          {
            "section_type": "example_question",
            "normalized_html": "<p>What value of <span class=\"math\">[MATH: b]</span> satisfies the equation <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 9b - 81 = 108?]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "What value of [MATH: b] satisfies the equation [MATH: 9b - 81 = 108?]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>EXPLANATION</p>",
            "readable_text": "EXPLANATION",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "example_explanation",
            "normalized_html": "<p>We are given the equation <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 9b - 81 = 108]</span> and are asked to solve for <span class=\"math\">[MATH: b.]</span></p><p>To isolate the term <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 9b,]</span> we add <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 81]</span> to both sides of the equation\n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: 9b|= 108 + 81; = 189.]</span></p><p>Now, we divide both sides by <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 9]</span>\n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: b|= (189)/(9); = 21.]</span></p><p>So, the value of <span class=\"math\">[MATH: b]</span> that satisfies the equation is <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 21.]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "We are given the equation [MATH: 9b - 81 = 108] and are asked to solve for [MATH: b.]\n\nTo isolate the term [MATH: 9b,] we add [MATH: 81] to both sides of the equation\n[MATH: 9b|= 108 + 81; = 189.]\n\nNow, we divide both sides by [MATH: 9]\n[MATH: b|= (189)/(9); = 21.]\n\nSo, the value of [MATH: b] that satisfies the equation is [MATH: 21.]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          }
        ],
        "images": [],
        "free_entry_blanks": [],
        "select_lists": [],
        "readable_text": "Example Prompt:\nWhat value of [MATH: b] satisfies the equation [MATH: 9b - 81 = 108?]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nWe are given the equation [MATH: 9b - 81 = 108] and are asked to solve for [MATH: b.]\n\nTo isolate the term [MATH: 9b,] we add [MATH: 81] to both sides of the equation\n[MATH: 9b|= 108 + 81; = 189.]\n\nNow, we divide both sides by [MATH: 9]\n[MATH: b|= (189)/(9); = 21.]\n\nSo, the value of [MATH: b] that satisfies the equation is [MATH: 21.]"
