    "readable_text": "Item 1 \u2014 Tutorial: Introduction\n\nContent:\nIn this topic, we'll practice solving multistep linear equations. You may also be asked to evaluate an expression using your solution.\n\n---\n\nItem 2 \u2014 Example: Solving Two-Step Equations Containing Larger Numbers\n\nExample Prompt:\nWhat value of [MATH: b] satisfies the equation [MATH: 9b - 81 = 108?]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nWe are given the equation [MATH: 9b - 81 = 108] and are asked to solve for [MATH: b.]\n\nTo isolate the term [MATH: 9b,] we add [MATH: 81] to both sides of the equation\n[MATH: 9b|= 108 + 81; = 189.]\n\nNow, we divide both sides by [MATH: 9]\n[MATH: b|= (189)/(9); = 21.]\n\nSo, the value of [MATH: b] that satisfies the equation is [MATH: 21.]\n\n---\n\nItem 3 \u2014 Question 1\n\nPrompt:\nWhat value of [MATH: p] satisfies the equation [MATH: 6p \u2212 18 = 60?]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: 11]\nb. [MATH: 10]\nc. [MATH: 13]\nd. [MATH: 18]\ne. [MATH: 16]\n\n---\n\nItem 4 \u2014 Question 2\n\nPrompt:\nWhat value of [MATH: r] satisfies the equation [MATH: 7r \u2212 35 = 119?]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: 14]\nb. [MATH: 28]\nc. [MATH: 35]\nd. [MATH: 22]\ne. [MATH: 42]\n\n---\n\nItem 5 \u2014 Example: Solving Two-Step Equations (Free-Response)\n\nExample Prompt:\n[MATH: 6r - 18 = 180]\nWhat is the solution to the given equation?\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nWe are given the equation [MATH: 6r - 18 = 180] and are asked to solve for [MATH: r.]\n\nLet's solve the equation for [MATH: r{:}]\n[MATH: 6r \u2212 18|= 180; 6r|= 180 + 18; 6r|= 198; r|= (198)/(6); r|= 33]\n\n---\n\nItem 6 \u2014 Question 3\n\nPrompt:\n[MATH: 3y \u2212 4 = 92]\nWhat is the solution to the given equation?[MATH: y =]\n[FREE_ENTRY 1]\n\n---\n\nItem 7 \u2014 Question 4\n\nPrompt:\n[MATH: 6r \u2212 18 = 180]\nWhat is the solution to the given equation?[MATH: r =]\n[FREE_ENTRY 1]\n\n---\n\nItem 8 \u2014 Example: Solving a Two-Step Equation and Evaluating an Expression\n\nExample Prompt:\nIf [MATH: 6p + 8 = 26,] what is the value of [MATH: 2p - 3?]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nWe are given the equation [MATH: 6p + 8 = 26] and are asked to find the value of [MATH: 2p - 3.]\n\nFirst, we solve the equation for [MATH: p{:}]\n[MATH: 6p + 8|= 26; 6p|= 18; p|= 3]\n\nNow, we substitute [MATH: p = 3] into [MATH: 2p - 3{:}]\n[MATH: 2p \u2212 3|= 2(3) \u2212 3; = 6 \u2212 3; = 3]\n\nTherefore, the value of [MATH: 2p - 3] is [MATH: 3.]\n\n---\n\nItem 9 \u2014 Question 5\n\nPrompt:\nIf [MATH: 6x \u2212 4 = 8,] what is the value of [MATH: 12x \u2212 2?]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: 8]\nb. [MATH: 26]\nc. [MATH: 30]\nd. [MATH: 22]\ne. [MATH: 2]\n\n---\n\nItem 10 \u2014 Question 6\n\nPrompt:\nIf [MATH: 6p + 8 = 26,] what is the value of [MATH: 2p \u2212 3?]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: 5]\nb. [MATH: 2]\nc. [MATH: 3]\nd. [MATH: 4]\ne. [MATH: 1]\n\n---\n\nItem 11 \u2014 Example: Solving a Two-Step Equation and Evaluating an Expression (Free-Response)\n\nExample Prompt:\nCalculate [MATH: 2d - 7] given that [MATH: 4d + 20 = 0.]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nWe are given the equation [MATH: 4d + 20 = 0] and are asked to find the value of [MATH: 2d - 7.]\n\nFirst, we solve the equation for [MATH: d{:}]\n[MATH: 4d + 20|= 0; 4d|= \u2212 20; d|= \u2212 5]\n\nNow that we know [MATH: d = -5,] we substitute this value into the expression [MATH: 2d - 7] and simplify:\n[MATH: 2d \u2212 7|= 2(\u2212 5) \u2212 7; = \u2212 10 \u2212 7; = \u2212 17]\n\n---\n\nItem 12 \u2014 Question 7\n\nPrompt:\nIf [MATH: 4x \u2212 5 = 11,] then [MATH: 8x + 2 =][FREE_ENTRY 1].\n\n---\n\nItem 13 \u2014 Question 8\n\nPrompt:\nIf [MATH: 4d + 20 = 0,] then [MATH: 2d \u2212 7 =][FREE_ENTRY 1]."
